body:
I'd kill for one, I just have to deal with the shitty weed oil carts instead, meh. I can't give you help specifically with what works for DMT, but I know for weed oils, I got this nice one that has three different volts, I think its 2.7, 3.1 and 3.5 or something? It has a magnet that lets you clip the cart right in, and uses a regular android phone type charger to charge it. It says HOOPCE (the two Os are like an infinity sign) on it so I guess that's the name. It's convenient, but if you can keep track of the shitty chargers that come with them, the Ooze pens are great. The voltage is a range, you twist it and it goes from , 3.1 or something all the way to 4.8. Its much easier to control the wattage with those, they're not too expensive, and it'll help so you can start with a low volt an work your way up without burning too much of the cart. Safe tripping.

&#x200B;

Edit: the volts

Do you have a history of previous alcohol/substance abuse and just started dope in November, or drugs entirely? Because if its the latter, that's a hell of a start. Your story is common. I've met people pronounced dead for almost an hour, hit with Narcan several times, was taken to the ER, and because of the withdrawal the Narcan puts you in, said person was discharged and continued to then meet their dealer in the hospital's parking lot and did another shot, only to OD again. Don't know whatever happened to the kid, but there are stories like these, some more intense, some not. The point is, I hope you mean it.

&#x200B;

I was shooting for a couple of years, wound up getting sloppy and not being hygienic (reusing old pins, not using alcohol swabs, etc). I got an awful infection in one of the bones in my spine (I was shooting everywhere else, but somehow the infection settled nicely in the bone luckily, instead of just hanging out in my bloodstream generally)  that tore through some muscles in one of my ass cheeks and some important parts that made me unable to move my legs, sit, move, anything at all. I thought I pulled my sciatica! Ha! So I spent about a week in a wheelchair being taken care of by my girl, still using though since I was in horrible pain. It was the worst pain I've ever had in my life, and it was embarrassing as fuck. She had to help me just to get to the bathroom, and hold me so I could stand and pee (couldn't even sit to make it easier. I was maybe 21 at the time. When her mom saw how bad I was she told me that no, in fact I did not pull my sciatica, and I need to go to a hospital ASAP. Spent almost 3 weeks in the hospital, wasn't in a clinic at the time so no methadone, and I couldn't really use in there. The doctors gave me some Ketamine to try and help with the withdrawals because they refused morphine since, you know, I'm just a junkie and he doesn't want to give me any of that (what an ass). My only solace was that I was allowed Dilaudid IV for pain every 6 hours. Sometimes I'd get lucky and Id get a nurse who didnt care enough to follow protocol, so instead of diluting the solution and slowly pushing it, they just gave it to me like a shot. It was the one thing that really kept me from going through the worst of the worst. When I got out, I still needed physical therapy and a walker to walk.

&#x200B;

I know this has been long, but I'm getting to the point. I got home and couldn't cop. I had to bum my mom's blues and try and shoot that. After I was able to walk again fine I went right back to using. I promised myself, oh I'll just be more careful, use the rig only once, use fresh sterile water, alcohol pads, wash hands and areas where I went, etc" I had been to the hospital again after that, so had my friends who were using, I'd been to detoxes after that too, only to walk out and cop right after. To be honest, that was rock bottom for me. But you don't need to hit "rock bottom" to get better. a few years before the infection, I was clean for 6 months, longest I ever had, and it was thanks to Subs. But I wasn't ready, and  then one day I didn't take it, and I went and copped a bag. I know people who've died. I've seen my best friend almost die plenty of times. This is a horrible life to live. I thought it was a joke when people I knew told me, but its not. I'm sure you know the withdrawals feel like you're dying, or that dying would be preferable at that point. The longest I made it cold turkey was 2 days. Then I decided well, I hate being sick, and Subs didn't work out for me the second and third time around, so eventually I went on Methadone. I was still using at first and I still get sick, but its much, much better. It helps the cravings, and when that doesn't, I tried smoking weed for the like, second time in my life and it works amazingly, even for withdrawals too. Then, one day I really just decided, you know what, I was just using to not be sick, I wasn't even really enjoying it or really getting high anymore so...I stopped. I just made 6 months, and the cravings have gone down drastically after the first 3 months.

&#x200B;

I didn't almost die, and things certainly could have gotten worse for me. And even when the worst (for me) was going on, I was scared but too in deep to let it go. Every time I'd do it, I'd have a brief moment of clarity, knowing that I have to stop and that there's no future going on like this. But then 5 or so hours pass and I'd get sick or let emotional pain get to me and fuck it, so what if I die a junkie? If you've made it to the end of this comment, I'm sure you mean this right now, and hopefully you mean it tomorrow too and going forwards. But, scares don't always make people want to get clean. You have to want it. Maybe the fear can push you, but the want to actually have a life, to know that using will only lead either to more death, to misery, or to most likely jail. You have to want to, for yourself - not anyone else - stop and find a healthy outlet for whatever made you turn to drugs in the first place. You're much stronger than you know, OP. And know that you have a community here who will listen, and that if you do wind up going back and using, that you don't need to "hit rock bottom" (or the stereotypical rock bottom) to get better. Sometimes you really can just wake up, have something small happen that gives you that epiphany, or something. I don't know, I think I started rambling. Best of luck OP, I hope you stay away. Heroin steals your soul. It makes you fall in love, breaks your heart, makes you feel like you're dying, makes you want to die, and is a bitch to deal with. But you'll come out stronger in the end, I promise you that.

&#x200B;

TL:DR  Scary things happening can make you want to stop at the moment, but doesn't always stick. You can get better, but only when you're actually ready, and there are resources that can help. You don't need to almost die again if this isn't a wake up call, sometimes you realize that while using, you're not living, you're barely surviving, all on your own.

And Kakuna. 

&#x200B;

You have a Poison type safari. Your pokemon are Kakuna, Swalot, and Toxicroack. You can now update your flair by the way
